## Initial Q&A
### Did a court or regulatory body in the United States legally ban Eric Trump, Donald Trump Jr., and Ivanka Trump from ever operating a charity again?
Answer: No, a court or regulatory body in the United States did not legally ban Eric Trump, Donald Trump Jr., or Ivanka Trump from operating a charity. According to the final resolution of the New York Supreme Court case, the court "did not bar either President Trump or his children Eric and Ivanka, from running charities in the state of New York." Instead, Eric and Ivanka Trump were only required to undergo "an in-person, interactive board training session pertaining to charitable organizations and the fiduciary responsibilities of those organizations' directors and officers."

Source URL: https://www.snopes.com/fact-check/trump-steal-kids-cancer-charity/

### What were the specific terms of the 2019 settlement between the New York Attorney General and the Trump family regarding the dissolution of the Donald J. Trump Foundation?
Answer: Under the terms of the 2019 settlement, the Donald J. Trump Foundation was dissolved, and Donald Trump was ordered to pay $2 million in damages. These damages, along with the foundation's remaining $1.78 million in assets, were distributed equally among eight different nonprofit organizations. Additionally, Donald Trump was placed under "ongoing supervision" by the New York Attorney General's office, and his children—Donald Jr., Eric, and Ivanka Trump—were required to "undergo compulsory training to ensure this type of illegal activity never takes place again."

Source URL: https://www.commondreams.org/news/2019/11/07/2-million-and-compulsory-training-presidents-children-called-poetic-end-trump

